        "math_academy_id": "q-281566",
        "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $\u25b3{P}^{\u2032}{Q}^{\u2032}{R}^{\u2032}$, the image of $\u25b3PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{\u2032}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{\u2032}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{\u2032}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the image of $\u25b3PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\u25b3{P}^{\u2032}{Q}^{\u2032}{R}^{\u2032}$ are ${P}^{\u2032}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{\u2032}(18,8),$ ${R}^{\u2032}(-8,-4).$",
